```mdl
test QA-9: Hello Worker — the agent finishes the spec, plans the work and ships the Worker
  desc: |
    The Hello Worker template run on camera. The space holds a partial spec, the project's feature map and three
    planning tasks; one chat assigned all three completes the spec in Composer, draws it on the canvas, files the
    implementation as tasks of its own linked to the features, and works them until the deployed Worker answers.
    The take never shows the chat, which carries the claim URL, a bearer credential. Recorded by
    autocue/hello-worker.mjs.
  actors: human
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists, on a fresh profile, talking to an EDGE whose AI and sandbox services serve the chosen model
    - plugin-debug, Code and Sandbox are enabled (dev-only defaults); Illustrator and Canvas are on by default
  steps:
    - name: Create a space from the Hello Worker template
      do: Add a space and pick the "Hello Worker" template.
      expect: the space opens with the "Hello Worker" project in the navtree
    - name: Open the project and its tasks
      do: Open the project and its Tasks tab.
      expect: three todo tasks, "Complete the spec", "Draw the proposed architecture", "Plan the implementation as tasks"
    - name: Open the feature map and the spec
      do: Open the Features tab as Kanban, then "Greeting endpoint" and its spec row.
      expect: four planned features; the spec renders in Composer with F-1 written and F-2 to F-4 only named
    - name: Assign the planning tasks to the agent
      do: Back on Tasks, tick all three and assign them to the agent.
      expect: the Gantt opens with one band for the chat and a lane for each task
    - name: Watch the spec fill in
      do: Wait for "Complete the spec", then open the spec.
      expect: the spec has a `feat` block for each of F-2 to F-4 and a new Changelog decision
    - name: Open the diagram from the project
      do: Wait for the diagram task, then open the project's Overview and the drawing.
      expect: a drawing of the sandbox, the Worker, the temporary Cloudflare account and the client's request and JSON response
    - name: Watch the plan become tasks
      do: Back on Tasks, wait for the plan task.
      expect: new implementation tasks under the plan, each linked on the feature map; the claim is assigned to you
    - name: Watch the Worker ship
      do: Wait for the agent's implementation tasks.
      expect: every task but the claim done or in review, and the Worker URL and its response filed on the project

test QA-10: Ride Check — spec, diagram, deploy, edit a feature card, redeploy
  desc: |
    The Ride Check template as a demo of the whole loop. The space holds a written spec, a feature map with one card
    per card on the page and three tasks. The take creates the space, reads the feature map and the spec, draws the
    architecture, shows the deployed page, then adds a gust rule to the Go / no-go card, redeploys and reloads the
    same URL. Recorded in two halves: autocue/ride-check.mjs in Composer and autocue/ride-check-redeploy.mjs on the
    page and the terminal, spliced into one cut.
  actors: human
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists, on a fresh profile
    - plugin-debug, Code and Sandbox are enabled (dev-only defaults); Illustrator and Canvas are on by default
    - the Worker is deployed at its v1 (ride-check/prepare.sh), with the gust rule committed but not deployed
  steps:
    - name: Create a space from the Ride Check template
      do: Add a space and pick the "Ride Check" template.
      expect: the space opens with the "Ride Check" project in the navtree
    - name: Open the feature map
      do: Open the project's Features tab.
      expect: four planned cards, "Go / no-go", "Hourly forecast", "Best window", "Daylight"
    - name: Open the spec
      do: Open "Go / no-go" and its spec row.
      expect: the spec renders in Composer with F-1 to F-4 written
    - name: Draw the architecture
      do: Run "Draw the architecture" (the agent, or the Drawing skill's draw operation with the diagram source).
      expect: a drawing of the browser, the Worker with its four cards, and Open-Meteo, filed on the project
    - name: Open the live page
      do: Open the Worker URL for a place with calm wind and gusts over 30 km/h.
      expect: the verdict reads GO and lists no gusts
    - name: Add the gust rule to the card
      do: On "Go / no-go", add the subfeature "Gust rule — warn above 30 km/h".
      expect: the card shows three subfeatures
    - name: Redeploy and reload
      do: Deploy the gust-rule commit and reload the same URL.
      expect: the verdict reads MAYBE with "Gusts up to N km/h" and a highlighted Gusts row
```

## Changelog

Every change to this spec adds a decision, newest last. See `lang/changelog.mdl` for the attribution rules.

```mdl
decision D-1: [QA-9] records the Hello Worker template from a partial spec, feature map and planning tasks: the assistant completes the spec, draws it, files the implementation as tasks and works them until the Worker answers.
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [QA-9]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The take assigns all three planning tasks to one chat and never shows the chat, which carries the claim URL. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-21
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [QA-9]
  why: One chat keeps the spec it wrote in its context when it plans and builds; the claim URL is a bearer credential for the account.
  rejected: Stopping before the deploy, as the take did before, which would not show the Worker answering.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: [QA-10] demos the loop with the Ride Check template, a ride-forecast page built with DXOS UI on live Open-Meteo data, in place of [QA-9]'s JSON greeting.
  date: 2026-10-27
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [QA-10]
  why: Every step of the loop has to change something a viewer can see; a greeting endpoint gives the deploy and the edit nothing to show.
  rejected: Rewriting Hello Worker in place, which its eval, QA-9 and the showcase speaking track still describe.
```
